Feature: SQL Aggregation of Sales Data for Specified Brands, Products, Markets, and Conditions

  The system must aggregate sales data from the bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack_weekly table in Unity Catalog purgo_databricks, schema purgo_playground, for each unique combination of brand_name, product_name, market_name, competitor_flag, channel, and transaction_time. The aggregation must sum integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars, applying specific business rules for brands and GPO flags, date filtering, and market inclusion.

  Background:
    Given the source table is purgo_databricks.purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack_weekly
    And the columns used are:
      | brand_name                | STRING  |
      | product_name              | STRING  |
      | market_name               | STRING  |
      | competitor_flag           | STRING  |
      | channel                   | STRING  |
      | transaction_time          | DATE    |
      | integrated_units          | NUMERIC |
      | integrated_normalized_units| NUMERIC |
      | integrated_dollars        | NUMERIC |
      | gpo_flag                  | STRING  |
      | cdl_effective_date        | DATE    |
    And the valid market_name values are "trastuzumab-anns", "bevacizumab-awwb", "rituximab market"
    And the valid brand_name values for zeroing sales are "kanjinti", "mvasi", "riabni"
    And the GPO flag must be checked for substring "KAISER" (case-insensitive)
    And transaction_time must be within the last 36 months from cdl_effective_date (inclusive)
    And aggregation is performed for each unique combination of brand_name, product_name, market_name, competitor_flag, channel, transaction_time

  Scenario Outline: Aggregate sales data for valid combinations and apply business rules
    Given a row with brand_name "<brand_name>", product_name "<product_name>", market_name "<market_name>", competitor_flag "<competitor_flag>", channel "<channel>", transaction_time "<transaction_time>", integrated_units <integrated_units>, integrated_normalized_units <integrated_normalized_units>, integrated_dollars <integrated_dollars>, gpo_flag "<gpo_flag>", cdl_effective_date "<cdl_effective_date>"
    When the market_name is one of "trastuzumab-anns", "bevacizumab-awwb", "rituximab market"
    And the transaction_time is within 36 months prior to and including cdl_effective_date
    And the brand_name is "<brand_name>"
    And the gpo_flag contains "KAISER" (case-insensitive)
    Then the aggregated integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars for this combination must be zero
    And the output must include the combination with zeroed values

    Examples:
      | brand_name | product_name | market_name        | competitor_flag | channel | transaction_time | integrated_units | integrated_normalized_units | integrated_dollars | gpo_flag         | cdl_effective_date |
      | kanjinti   | prodA        | trastuzumab-anns   | Y               | retail  | 2023-05-01       | 100              | 90                        | 1000              | KAISER PERM      | 2023-06-01         |
      | mvasi      | prodB        | bevacizumab-awwb   | N               | hospital| 2022-12-15       | 200              | 180                       | 2000              | kaiser           | 2023-01-01         |
      | riabni     | prodC        | rituximab market   | Y               | retail  | 2021-07-10       | 50               | 45                        | 500               | Kaiser Permanente| 2021-08-01         |

  Scenario Outline: Aggregate sales data for valid combinations without zeroing sales
    Given a row with brand_name "<brand_name>", product_name "<product_name>", market_name "<market_name>", competitor_flag "<competitor_flag>", channel "<channel>", transaction_time "<transaction_time>", integrated_units <integrated_units>, integrated_normalized_units <integrated_normalized_units>, integrated_dollars <integrated_dollars>, gpo_flag "<gpo_flag>", cdl_effective_date "<cdl_effective_date>"
    When the market_name is one of "trastuzumab-anns", "bevacizumab-awwb", "rituximab market"
    And the transaction_time is within 36 months prior to and including cdl_effective_date
    And (the brand_name is not "kanjinti", "mvasi", "riabni" OR the gpo_flag does not contain "KAISER" case-insensitive)
    Then the aggregated integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars for this combination must be the sum of the respective values
    And the output must include the combination with summed values

    Examples:
      | brand_name | product_name | market_name        | competitor_flag | channel | transaction_time | integrated_units | integrated_normalized_units | integrated_dollars | gpo_flag         | cdl_effective_date |
      | herceptin  | prodA        | trastuzumab-anns   | Y               | retail  | 2023-05-01       | 100              | 90                        | 1000              | ABC GPO          | 2023-06-01         |
      | mvasi      | prodB        | bevacizumab-awwb   | N               | hospital| 2022-12-15       | 200              | 180                       | 2000              | XYZ GPO          | 2023-01-01         |
      | riabni     | prodC        | rituximab market   | Y               | retail  | 2021-07-10       | 50               | 45                        | 500               | DEF GPO          | 2021-08-01         |

  Scenario Outline: Exclude rows with invalid market_name
    Given a row with market_name "<market_name>"
    When the market_name is not "trastuzumab-anns", "bevacizumab-awwb", or "rituximab market"
    Then the row must be excluded from aggregation
    And no output should be generated for this combination

    Examples:
      | market_name        |
      | abc-market         |
      | xyz-market         |
      | test-market        |

  Scenario Outline: Exclude rows with transaction_time outside 36 months window
    Given a row with transaction_time "<transaction_time>" and cdl_effective_date "<cdl_effective_date>"
    When transaction_time is more than 36 months before cdl_effective_date
    Then the row must be excluded from aggregation
    And no output should be generated for this combination

    Examples:
      | transaction_time | cdl_effective_date |
      | 2019-01-01       | 2023-06-01         |
      | 2018-05-15       | 2021-08-01         |
      | 2017-12-31       | 2021-12-31         |

  Scenario Outline: Error handling for missing required fields
    Given a row with missing "<missing_field>"
    When the aggregation is performed
    Then an error must be raised with message "Missing required field: <missing_field>"

    Examples:
      | missing_field      |
      | brand_name         |
      | product_name       |
      | market_name        |
      | competitor_flag    |
      | channel            |
      | transaction_time   |
      | integrated_units   |
      | integrated_normalized_units |
      | integrated_dollars |
      | gpo_flag           |
      | cdl_effective_date |

  Scenario Outline: Error handling for invalid data formats
    Given a row with "<field>" value "<invalid_value>"
    When the aggregation is performed
    Then an error must be raised with message "Invalid format for <field>: <invalid_value>"

    Examples:
      | field                | invalid_value      |
      | transaction_time     | not-a-date        |
      | cdl_effective_date   | 2023/06/01        |
      | integrated_units     | abc               |
      | integrated_dollars   | $1000             |
      | gpo_flag             | NULL              |

  Scenario: Aggregation uniqueness
    Given multiple rows with identical values for brand_name, product_name, market_name, competitor_flag, channel, transaction_time
    When the aggregation is performed
    Then the output must contain a single row for each unique combination
    And the integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars must be summed (or zeroed per business rule)

  Scenario: Case-insensitive matching for GPO flag "KAISER"
    Given a row with gpo_flag "kaiser permanente"
    When the brand_name is "kanjinti"
    Then the sales values must be zeroed
    And the output must reflect zeroed values

  Scenario: Case-sensitive brand_name matching
    Given a row with brand_name "KANJINTI" (all caps)
    When the gpo_flag contains "KAISER"
    Then the sales values must NOT be zeroed
    And the output must reflect the actual summed values

  Scenario: Output column order and format
    Given the aggregation is complete
    Then the output must include columns in the following order:
      | brand_name |
      | product_name |
      | market_name |
      | competitor_flag |
      | channel |
      | transaction_time |
      | integrated_units |
      | integrated_normalized_units |
      | integrated_dollars |
    And all numeric values must be in standard decimal format
    And all date values must be in YYYY-MM-DD format
